WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.545 --> 00:00:13.345
Izzie hurried toward Kids Central.

2
00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:18.088
She saw Nina, Jason, and Ethan in the hallway.

3
00:00:18.089 --> 00:00:20.654
"You're back!" Nina said.

4
00:00:20.655 --> 00:00:23.491
"Miss Shelly said you were sick."

5
00:00:23.492 --> 00:00:28.394
"I was sick," Izzie said. "I had the flu."

6
00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:33.505
"My dad has it now," Jason said. "He's miserable."

7
00:00:33.506 --> 00:00:37.816
"Everybody is getting sick," Izzie said.

8
00:00:37.817 --> 00:00:40.078
The kids walked into the gym.

9
00:00:40.079 --> 00:00:42.821
Suddenly everyone halted.

10
00:00:42.822 --> 00:00:48.026
"Mr. Dunn?" Izzie said. "What are you doing here?"

11
00:00:48.027 --> 00:00:52.720
Mr. Dunn laughed. "Aren't you happy to see me?"

12
00:00:52.721 --> 00:00:56.129
"Of course we are!" Nina said.

13
00:00:56.130 --> 00:01:00.968
Bobby raced into the gym. "Mr. Dunn?"

14
00:01:00.969 --> 00:01:04.314
"Miss Shelly has the flu," Mr. Dunn said.

15
00:01:04.315 --> 00:01:06.864
"So you're stuck with me today."

16
00:01:06.865 --> 00:01:10.801
All the kids laughed, except Nina.

17
00:01:10.802 --> 00:01:14.266
"What's the matter, Nina?" Mr. Dunn asked.

18
00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:17.122
"I'm happy you're here," Nina said.

19
00:01:17.123 --> 00:01:20.396
"But I'm sad Miss Shelly is sick."

20
00:01:20.397 --> 00:01:23.531
"Me too," Izzie said.

21
00:01:23.532 --> 00:01:28.187
"Maybe we can do something nice for her," Mr. Dunn said.

22
00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:31.631
"My mom makes soup when I'm sick," Jason said.

23
00:01:31.632 --> 00:01:36.257
"We don't have any ingredients for soup," Mr. Dunn said.

24
00:01:36.258 --> 00:01:39.903
"We can make cards," Nina suggested.

25
00:01:39.904 --> 00:01:43.093
"I have a better idea," Izzie said.

26
00:01:43.094 --> 00:01:46.202
"Let's make a 'get well' jar!"

27
00:01:46.203 --> 00:01:48.776
"What's that?" Ethan asked.

28
00:01:48.777 --> 00:01:53.200
"It's a jar filled with things that cheer you up," Izzie said.

29
00:01:53.201 --> 00:01:55.788
"My grandmother sent me one when I was sick.

30
00:01:55.789 --> 00:02:00.045
It had playing cards, tissues, and hard candies.

31
00:02:00.046 --> 00:02:03.429
And frog treats for Gurpy!"

32
00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:06.083
"Sounds good," Bobby said.

33
00:02:06.084 --> 00:02:08.743
"But where are we going to get a jar?"

34
00:02:08.744 --> 00:02:12.068
"And frog food?" Jason asked.

35
00:02:12.069 --> 00:02:14.053
Mr. Dunn laughed.

36
00:02:14.054 --> 00:02:20.708
"I'll look in the supply closet and see what I can find."

37
00:02:20.709 --> 00:02:25.065
A few minutes later he returned.

38
00:02:25.066 --> 00:02:31.840
He had construction paper, markers, stickers, ribbon, and a large jar with a lid.

39
00:02:31.841 --> 00:02:35.965
"You found everything we need!" Izzie said.

40
00:02:35.966 --> 00:02:38.801
"Now what?" Jason asked.

41
00:02:38.802 --> 00:02:43.500
"First, everyone makes a get well card," Izzie said.

42
00:02:43.501 --> 00:02:47.154
The kids got to work making cards for Miss Shelly.

43
00:02:47.155 --> 00:02:50.580
When they were finished, Izzie reached for the jar.

44
00:02:50.581 --> 00:02:54.317
"Now we add goodies to the jar."

45
00:02:54.318 --> 00:02:57.202
"I have some cough drops," Ethan said.

46
00:02:57.203 --> 00:02:59.665
"And two lollipops."

47
00:02:59.666 --> 00:03:03.010
"I have a pack of tissues," Jason said.

48
00:03:03.011 --> 00:03:05.638
"And dog stickers."

49
00:03:05.639 --> 00:03:08.047
Nina looked in her backpack.

50
00:03:08.048 --> 00:03:13.209
"I found some grape lip balm. It's brand-new!"

51
00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:17.972
Mr. Dunn added some tea bags to the jar and a package of cookies.

52
00:03:17.973 --> 00:03:21.005
"What about you, Bobby?" Izzie asked.

53
00:03:21.006 --> 00:03:23.582
"What will you add to the jar?"

54
00:03:23.583 --> 00:03:25.419
Bobby shrugged.

55
00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:30.679
Izzie frowned. "You have to contribute something."

56
00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:34.611
"Bobby made a beautiful card," Mr. Dunn said.

57
00:03:34.612 --> 00:03:37.856
"And I think we have plenty of stuff."

58
00:03:37.857 --> 00:03:42.498
"Okay, but the jar isn't finished yet," Izzie said.

59
00:03:42.499 --> 00:03:45.881
"Now I need to decorate it."

60
00:03:45.882 --> 00:03:49.478
"Can't we all do it?" Nina asked.

61
00:03:49.479 --> 00:03:54.193
Mr. Dunn nodded. "Miss Shelly would like that."

62
00:03:54.194 --> 00:03:56.751
"Okay," Izzie mumbled.

63
00:03:56.752 --> 00:04:00.875
"Sorry that I was being a little bossy."

64
00:04:00.876 --> 00:04:03.933
The kids started decorating the jar.

65
00:04:03.934 --> 00:04:09.621
They used ribbon, stickers, and some fabric.

66
00:04:09.622 --> 00:04:13.229
"It looks beautiful!" Nina said.

67
00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:14.801
Mr. Dunn nodded.

68
00:04:14.802 --> 00:04:18.041
"This was a very thoughtful idea, Izzie.

69
00:04:18.042 --> 00:04:21.304
I'll drop the jar off at Miss Shelly's house later.

70
00:04:21.305 --> 00:04:23.753
It's going to cheer her up."

71
00:04:23.754 --> 00:04:32.771
Izzie smiled. "Especially since we made it together!"
